Original commit body from 3c7f5a1e4f38026099faac19d967de397ac826fb:

The producer-side axis walker resolved a kind= / edge_type= / evidence_type=
argument only when it reached a literal, a ternary, an f-string, or a Name
bound to one. A Subscript RHS poisoned resolution outright, and a tuple
assignment target was never inspected at all -- so both

    edge_type = MAP[k]
    suffix, edge_type = MAP[k]

shipped values the gate could not see. That is the exact blind spot behind
WI-rorul, whose OTP linker sent unregistered otp_call/otp_cast through
`handler_suffix, edge_type = CALL_TYPE_MAP[call_type]` while
test_no_strict_producer_violations_for_edge_type stayed green.

The walker now resolves a subscript over a module-level or function-local
dict display (LEGB order, nearest binding scope wins) to the union of its
literal string values, indexing per-position for tuple-unpack targets --
at the assignment form and at the bare `edge_type=MAP[k]` kwarg site, so
gate coverage no longer depends on whether the producer bound a local
first. The key is deliberately not resolved: every value the map can yield
is a candidate, the sound over-approximation for a gate.

The conservative posture is unchanged and load-bearing. One non-literal map
value, a starred unpack target, a value tuple shorter than the unpack index,
a non-Name subscript base, or an empty map is a silent skip -- never a
partial candidate set, which would let the gate report "clean" on a map
whose unresolvable branch is precisely the one shipping an unregistered
value.

NOT preventive-only as filed. The item recorded "ZERO current exploiter"
(WI-rorul having folded the only known one). On its first run the hardened
gate flagged Symbol.kind="scalar", emitted by the GraphQL analyzer's
type_kinds dict -- the sole unregistered member of a six-way sibling set
(type/input/interface/enum/union all registered). The cause is
self-referential: the corpus enumeration audit-findings 0007 was built from
could not see dict-indirected emits, so the value was structurally
invisible for exactly as long as the walker was blind to MAP[k].

scalar is registered as a language_construct rather than folded: `scalar Date`
is its own GraphQL type-system construct, and `type` is already taken by
object_type_definition in that same dict, so conflating them would fuse two
distinct constructs (ADR-0027 apex/peer). This follows the mutation /
subscription precedent -- same analyzer, same audit-omission cause.

Also: spec section 6's registry count corrected 143 -> 152 (drifted
independently of this change); schema.json and concept-axes.md regenerated;
the schema-coverage baseline picks up scalar and sheds 29 dead entries left
behind by the endpoint_shape prune (shrink-only, no toleration loosened).

